# Finding 3 (RESULTS.md), a new candidate and a clock effect: the wall clock steps back by a day
# before step 7, and a kill of the stream's writer before step 13 leaves the stream s without a
# writer for the size of the step. Every node runs with multi_time_warp, so a node that ran
# before the step keeps its system time a day ahead until its next check of the OS clock.
# rabbit3 is killed before step 7 (to cut a file of its quorum queue WAL) and starts again
# before step 9, after the step, with its clock right. The writer rabbit1, also the stream
# coordinator's leader, is killed before step 13 and is back before step 15. The new leader
# rabbit2 parks the failed restarts of the replicas on rabbit2 and rabbit3 with a retry time of
# its own system time, still a day ahead, plus 5 to 10 s. After its check the retries are a day
# away, and rabbit1's member, woken by its nodeup, is no quorum alone. Every stream publish then
# answers "Leader not Ready yet", and eventually_probe fails 60 s after the faults. Found blind
# by `hydo explore` (e3's seed 10, with the kill before step 12 on that image). On this image
# hydo 0.7.0 gave one fingerprint twice, and without T=, without K= or without G= (and its
# restart of rabbit3) the run passes. The kill before step 10, 11 or 12 passes, and so does the
# kill before step 13 with the step before step 8.
# expect: violation      (change to ok when the bug is fixed)
disk=none dseed=0 | run K=nodes.primary@13+2 N=rabbit1-*@14-20:delay,402ms P=rabbit3@2+3 T=7:-86400 W=a36fcf62,p3,q2,r2000 G=rabbit3@7+2:trunc,seed=8657d94c
